-- title:
--   Vacuum certificate for a coordinate metric on an open domain
-- statement:
--   For coordinate metrics $g,\hat g$ on $\mathbb R^{n+1}$ and a set $U\subseteq\mathbb R^{n+1}$, the proposition $\mathrm{VacuumCertificate}(g,\hat g,U)$ is the conjunction of eight obligations: (1) $U$ is open; (2) $U$ is nonempty; (3) $g_{ij}(x)=g_{ji}(x)$ for all $x\in U$; (4) $\hat g(x)\,g(x)=I$ for all $x\in U$; (5) every $g_{ij}$ is $C^\infty$ on $U$; (6) every $\hat g^{ij}$ is $C^\infty$ on $U$; (7) $g(x)$ is Lorentzian for all $x\in U$; (8) $R_{bd}(x)=0$ for all $x\in U$ and all $b,d$, where $R$ is the coordinate Ricci tensor of $(g,\hat g)$ from bundle `Atlas_Core_Basic`. The data $g,\hat g,U$ are supplied independently of any proof, so a certificate is never vacuous by construction.
--
--   The acceptance criterion of every row of the atlas; each field is discharged by a separate theorem. Obligation (4) rules out a trivialising wrong inverse, (5)–(6) make every slice derivative in $R_{bd}$ a genuine derivative.
